{"id":25,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"Possesses cheek sacs in which it stores electricity. This clever forest-dweller roasts tough berries with an electric shock before consuming them."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"When Pikachu meet, they’ll touch their tails together and exchange electricity through them as a form of greeting."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Pikachu that can generate powerful electricity have cheek sacs that are extra soft and super stretchy."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"This forest-dwelling Pokémon stores electricity in its cheeks, so you’ll feel a tingly shock if you touch it."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"While sleeping, it generates electricity in the sacs in its cheeks. If it’s not getting enough sleep, it will be able to use only weak electricity."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It’s in its nature to store electricity. It feels stressed now and then if it’s unable to fully discharge the electricity."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"A plan was recently announced to gather many Pikachu and make an electric power plant."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"This Pokémon has electricity-storing pouches on its cheeks. These appear to become electrically charged during the night while Pikachu sleeps. It occasionally discharges electricity when it is dozy after waking up."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Whenever Pikachu comes across something new, it blasts it with a jolt of electricity. If you come across a blackened berry, it’s evidence that this Pokémon mistook the intensity of its charge."},{"games":["Y","FireRed"],"text":"It has small electric sacs on both its cheeks. If threatened, it looses electric charges from the sacs."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"It raises its tail to check its surroundings. The tail is sometimes struck by lightning in this pose."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"It occasionally uses an electric shock to recharge a fellow Pikachu that is in a weakened state."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"This intelligent Pokémon roasts hard berries with electricity to make them tender enough to eat."},{"games":["Pearl"],"text":"If it looses crackling power from the electric pouches on its cheeks, it is being wary."},{"games":["Diamond"],"text":"It lives in forests with others. It stores electricity in the pouches on its cheeks."},{"games":["LeafGreen"],"text":"When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity can build and cause lightning storms."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It stores electricity in the electric sacs on its cheeks. When it releases pent-up energy in a burst, the electric power is equal to a lightning bolt."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"When it is angered, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks."},{"games":["Yellow"],"text":"It keeps its tail raised to monitor its surroundings. If you yank its tail, it will try to bite you."},{"games":["Blue","Red"],"text":"When several of these POKéMON gather, their electricity could build and cause lightning storms."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Static","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon is charged with static electricity and may paralyze attackers that make direct contact with it."},{"name":"Lightning Rod","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon draws in all Electric-type moves. Instead of taking damage from them, its Sp. Atk stat is boosted."}],"eggGroups":["Field","Fairy"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":10,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"forest","color":"Yellow","shape":"Quadruped","evolution":{"id":172,"name":"Pichu","condition":null,"children":[{"id":25,"name":"Pikachu","condition":"Level up, High Friendship","children":[{"id":26,"name":"Raichu","condition":"Use Thunder Stone or Use Thunder Stone, in Alola","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,39],[1,45],[1,84],[1,98],[1,186],[1,204],[1,417],[1,589],[1,609],[4,86],[8,104],[12,486],[16,364],[20,209],[24,97],[28,231],[32,435],[36,85],[40,113],[44,87]],"machine":[97,914,34,280,268,451,204,91,574,577,598,604,486,527,227,283,203,263,313,374,264,447,270,282,113,417,583,182,240,115,156,179,214,164,57,129,36,851,168,87,9,86,85,885,918,521,528],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me55-149","name":"Pikachu ex","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Special Illustration Rare","number":"149","artist":"kantaro","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-149/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-149/large"},{"id":"me55-23","name":"Pikachu","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Pikachu Rare","number":"23","artist":"Ken Sugimori","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-23/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-23/large"},{"id":"me55-24","name":"Pikachu","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Pikachu Rare","number":"24","artist":"danciao","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-24/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-24/large"},{"id":"me55-25","name":"Pikachu","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Pikachu Rare","number":"25","artist":"satoma","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-25/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-25/large"},{"id":"me55-26","name":"Pikachu","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Pikachu Rare","number":"26","artist":"Takeshi Nakamura","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-26/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-26/large"},{"id":"me55-27","name":"Pikachu","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Pikachu Rare","number":"27","artist":"Asako Ito","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-27/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/p